title: Veeam: Restore points
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the restore points of a backup object (e.g. a virtual
 machine) of a Veeam Backup & Replication server, collected via the Veeam
 special agent. It reports the number of restore points, the age of the
 newest one, the platform, the object type, the type of the newest restore
 point and the malware status.

 This check is {CRIT} if the object has no restore point at all, since it
 cannot be recovered. {WARN} and {CRIT} levels can be set for the age of the
 newest restore point (default: 30 and 48 hours).

 The malware status is the worst one across all restore points of the
 object: {OK} if clean or informative, {WARN} if suspicious, {CRIT} if
 infected and {UNKNOWN} for any other value. This mapping is not
 configurable.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup object reported by the API.

item:
 The platform and the name of the backup object, e.g. {VMware - vm-1}. The
 name alone if the platform is unknown.
